[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 703,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 466,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107572,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 423,
        "headingId": 466,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Papillary cystadenoma is a benign papillary-cystic tumour of probable mesonephric origin, usually seen in patients with von&nbsp;Hippel&ndash;Lindau syndrome.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:55:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 704,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 467,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107573,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 423,
        "headingId": 467,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8450/0 Papillary cystadenoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:55:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 705,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 468,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107574,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 423,
        "headingId": 468,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F33.Y &amp; XH0FM6 Benign neoplasm of other specified female genital organs &amp; Papillary cystadenoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:55:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 706,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 469,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107575,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 423,
        "headingId": 469,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:55:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 707,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 470,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107576,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 423,
        "headingId": 470,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:55:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 708,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 471,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107577,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 423,
        "headingId": 471,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Uterine ligaments</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:55:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 709,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 472,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107578,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 423,
        "headingId": 472,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients may present with abdominal pain, although in children papillary cystadenoma is likely to be an incidental finding {22296276; 7977949}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:55:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 710,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 473,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107579,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 423,
        "headingId": 473,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most patients have von&nbsp;Hippel&ndash;Lindau syndrome {22296276; 22317868; 3341511; 2386149}. As yet this tumour has only been described in adults aged &gt;&nbsp;20&nbsp;years.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:55:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 711,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 474,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107580,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 423,
        "headingId": 474,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The anatomical location and immunophenotype suggest a mesonephric origin {22296276}. Allelic loss of <em>VHL</em> has been reported {11493991}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:55:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 712,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 475,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107581,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 423,
        "headingId": 475,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:55:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 719,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 482,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107582,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 423,
        "headingId": 482,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours are about 50&nbsp;mm (reported sizes range from &lt;&nbsp;10&nbsp;to 80&nbsp;mm), have a thick fibrotic capsule, and are traversed by fibrous bands creating a solid-cystic lobulated appearance {22296276; 9421096}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:55:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 713,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 476,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107583,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 423,
        "headingId": 476,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is complex tubulopapillary growth with varying broad-based and delicate branching and stromal hyalinization. Focal tubular or solid growth may be present. The cells are non-ciliated and cuboidal, with minimal clear to eosinophilic cytoplasm. Prominent subepithelial blood vessels are common. The cells are positive for CK7, PAX8, PAX2, and CD10. WT1 and calretinin are variably positive; ER and PR are negative {22296276; 22317868; 24441657; 15767808}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:55:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 714,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 477,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107584,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 423,
        "headingId": 477,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:55:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 715,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 478,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107585,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 423,
        "headingId": 478,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Demonstration of germline <em>VHL</em> mutation may be helpful.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:55:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 718,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 481,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107586,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 423,
        "headingId": 481,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a cystic/lobulated mass; complex tubulopapillary growth of non-ciliated and cuboidal cells.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> <em>VHL</em> mutation.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:55:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 716,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 479,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107587,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 423,
        "headingId": 479,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:55:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 717,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 480,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107588,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 423,
        "headingId": 480,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are benign, except for a single report of peritoneal metastases in a patient without von&nbsp;Hippel&ndash;Lindau syndrome {22296276}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:55:35"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]